# Keep the bundled demo data in the image despite the rules above. Note: demo/
# is gitignored (not committed), but the Docker *build context* comes from the
# working tree, not from git - so as long as demo/ exists on disk when you run
# `docker build`, it is copied into the image.
#
# To get demo/ onto a machine that lacks it, COPY IT (rsync/scp from a machine
# that has it - DEPLOYMENT.md, "Transferring the demo to a remote server").
# scripts/make_demo.py is NOT a general regeneration path: it derives the demo
# by trimming a full source model (data/HPM.zip plus the .hds runs, tens of GB)
# which is not present on a server or a fresh checkout. The shipped demo was
# transferred, not rebuilt.
!demo/
!demo/**
NEXT_STEPS.md
